  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="a628-61fa-20d3-6646" name="Late Imperial Roman (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #52 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). This army list represents the forces of the Roman Empire from the reign of Constantine I to the late 5th century and the overwhelming of Italy by the Ostrogoths. During this period the cavalry arm acquired more importance than it ever had in the Roman army, mainly due to the need to adapt to the enemies the Empire was facing. Academics are still debating on the quality of the Legios of the last centuries of the Western Empire and this list is just one of the possible interpretations. The list allows for the construction of a local border garrison force, an Imperial field army, and the forces of a Romanised warlord (probably with a Roman commission). Allies And Mercenaries: Any army may take allies from the Gothic &amp; Vandal Kingdoms list.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Late Imperial Roman - Border Garrison]
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Artillery: up to 20%
  Characters: Up to 25% Cavalry: Up to 25% Infantry: At least 50% Artillery: Up to 20%
[Late Imperial Roman - Imperial Field Army]
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Artillery: up to 20%
  Characters: Up to 25% Cavalry: Up to 50% Infantry: At least 25% Foederati: Up to 33% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: Up to 20% May have artillery fielded out of the Allies and mercenary point allocation.
[Late Imperial Roman - Romanised Warlord]
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Artillery: up to 20%
  Characters: Up to 25% Cavalry: Up to 50% Infantry: Up to 50% Foederati: At least 33%
[Late Imperial Roman - Romano-British]
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Artillery: up to 20%
  Characters: Up to 25% The army may not include an Imperator. Cavalry: Up to 50% May only take Equites. Infantry: At least 33% Foederati Infantry: Up to 33% There must be at least one Limitanei unit per unit of Legionaries. Any Foederati Infantry unit may be Open Order (+3).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
